Expanded story:
On a bright morning in their kitchen, Amy stirred eggs while Will and Amber laughed over pancakes on the counter. A sudden groan rattled the front door as a zombie burst through it, shuffling toward the living room.

Amy grabbed Will’s small hand first, then scooped up Amber beside him, pushing them into the back bedroom that served as their safe spot. She slammed the closet door shut behind them and hurried back to the kitchen in one breathless stride.

She slipped beneath the stove, pulling open a hidden drawer where her pistol gleamed alongside a polished katana. With both weapons in hand, she stepped out onto the hallway floor.

The zombie’s groan echoed as it turned toward Amy; she fired a quick shot that splintered its skull and then swung the katana to sever another with a swift slash. One by one, each new intruder met her gunfire or blade until the last of them fell, their bodies crumpling in a wet thud.

With the hallway empty, Amy turned back toward the bedroom she’d left behind, carrying Will and Amber out together as they stepped into the fresh air beyond the house.
